y possible sentence structure, but it is the most common one. “ku [sumti] kei [selbri] [sumti]” looks close, but “ku [sumti] kei” is not a valid pattern.“ku” terminates sumti (arguments) that are headed by the determiner “lo”. It does not preceded any sumti (arguments).“kei” is the terminator for various “abstraction particles”. It is out of place in this alleged pattern. -- Annotator 2 comment: {ku} and {kei} are terminators for LE (aka nominalizers, or 'gadri') and NU (aka content clause particles, or abstractors) respectively. They always go at the end.\n\nSentence 3: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: If “ku se ka vau kei” were a valid  sumti, or absent from the sentence, then #3 would be correct. -- Annotator 2 comment: {tunba} is the selbri (predicate) and {le ka stela vau kei se steba} is the sumti (argument).\n\nSentence 4: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: This does not make any sense. “se ka vau” does not exist in Lojban, but even if it did, the individual words that make it up have nothing to do with causality. -- Annotator 2 comment: {se} switches the places of slots in a predicate. {ka} is used to create a content clause about properties. {vau} is a terminator for bridi (assertions). To talk about causes, {se ja'e} should be used. Example: {se ja'e lo su'u stela} = \"because of the key\"\n\nSentence 5: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: False. (B) follows the basic pattern “[sumti] [selbri]”.“le ka stela vau kei se steba ku” is the sumti (argument), and “tunba” is the selbri (predicate). -- Annotator 2 comment: _see following comments_\n\nSentence 6: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: 1. “le ka” is a very common construction. 2. “ku tunba” is not a unit. The “ku” belongs to the sumti (argument) headed by “le”. In other words, the LLM is grouping the words incorrectly into sentence constituents. -- Annotator 2 comment: LE + NU is a very common construction in Lojban. All NU convert the contents within it into a selbri, which can then be converted into a sumti by LE.  Having {se steba} before {ku tunba} is grammatically valid.\n\nSentence 7: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: Incorrect argumentation and incorrect conclusion. -- Annotator 2 comment: _see previous comments_\n\n"}
