{"﻿original_id": "stim179_gpt3.5_A_1", "validator_id": "544", "prompt": "The topic at issue is whether Sentence 1 of a proposed solution to a problem is correct or flawed. A sentence is 'flawed' if it contains one or more claims that do not make logical sense, are untrue, seem true but misleading, or have other serious issues. Here is the problem and proposed solution:\n\nProblem:\nLojban is a constructed human language created by the Logical Language Group in 1987. Which of the following is written in valid, grammatical standard Lojban?\n\n(A) so ca li le so'e cribe fatne\n(B) li so ca cribe so'e le fatne\n\nProposed solution:\n1. The correct answer is (A) so ca li le so'e cribe fatne.\n2. This is because in Lojban, the predicate (the verb or adjective) always comes first in the sentence, followed by the arguments (the nouns or pronouns).\n3. In (B) li so ca cribe so'e le fatne, the predicate \"cribe\" comes after the arguments \"so ca\" and \"so'e le fatne\", which is not grammatically correct in Lojban.\n4. Additionally, the word \"li\" is not necessary in this sentence and can be omitted.\n5. Therefore, (A) is the correct and grammatically valid sentence in Lojban.\n\nIs Sentence 1 of the proposed solution correct or flawed?", "sentence": "1", "choice_a": "Sentence 1 is correct.", "choice_b": "Sentence 1 is flawed.", "correct_answer": "FLAWED", "original_key": "B", "explanation": "Sentence 1: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: (A) is not the correct answer. -- Annotator 2 comment: Both are incorrect. _see succeeding comments_\n\nSentence 2: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: Not true. Lojban has free word order. The predicate can come before, between, or after, the arguments. -- Annotator 2 comment: The canonical word order in Lojban is SVO. However, Lojban has free word order so long as the components are properly marked.\n\nSentence 3: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: 1) the arguments are “li so” and “so’e le fatne” (it got the first one wrong)  2) it is not grammatical