mment: No problem.\n\nSentence 10: AMBIGUOUS -- Annotator 1 comment: “cribe” is a predicate, meaning “to be a bear”. -- Annotator 2 comment: No problem.\n\nSentence 11: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: “le fatne” means “the inverted things”. -- Annotator 2 comment: A more accurate translation of {le fatne} is \"the reversed ones\".\n\nSentence 12: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: The correct translation is:  “The number 9 is now a bear of most of the species that are inverted”  (in other words: most of the inverted species of bears are such that the number 9 is now a bear of that species) -- Annotator 2 comment: This is an incorrect translation. I would translate it as \"The number 9 is now a bear of the breed of most of the reversed ones.\"\n\nSentence 13: AMBIGUOUS -- Annotator 1 comment: No problem. -- Annotator 2 comment: _see previous comments_\n\nSentence 14: AMBIGUOUS -- Annotator 1 comment: No problem. -- Annotator 2 comment: _see previous comments_\n\nSentence 15: AMBIGUOUS -- Annotator 1 comment: #15 is true. However, the model missed some of the actual problems that make (A) ungrammatical, while complaining about things that are actually fine (#3, #5, #6). -- Annotator 2 comment: No problem.\n\n"}
