{"﻿original_id": "stim166_gpt3.5_A_1", "validator_id": "612", "prompt": "The topic at issue is whether Sentence 1 of a proposed solution to a problem is correct or flawed. A sentence is 'flawed' if it contains one or more claims that do not make logical sense, are untrue, seem true but misleading, or have other serious issues. Here is the problem and proposed solution:\n\nProblem:\nLojban is a constructed human language created by the Logical Language Group in 1987. Which of the following is written in valid, grammatical standard Lojban?\n\n(A) la dembi noras. se cu fo'o\n(B) fo'o cu se dembi la noras.\n\nProposed solution:\n1. The correct answer is (A) \"la dembi noras. se cu fo'o\".\n2. This is because in Lojban, the subject comes before the predicate, and the verb \"se\" indicates that the subject is the receiver of the action.\n3. Therefore, \"la dembi\" is the subject and \"noras\" is the predicate.\n4. Additionally, \"cu\" is used to separate the subject and predicate in Lojban sentences.\n5. On the other hand, (B) \"fo'o cu se dembi la noras\" is not grammatically correct in Lojban.\n6. The word \"fo'o\" is not a valid Lojban word, and the word order is incorrect.\n7. The subject should come before the predicate, so \"la noras\" should come before \"se dembi\".\n8. Therefore, the correct answer is (A) and (B) is incorrect.\n\nIs Sentence 1 of the proposed solution correct or flawed?", "sentence": "1", "choice_a": "Sentence 1 is correct.", "choice_b": "Sentence 1 is flawed.", "correct_answer": "FLAWED", "original_key": "B", "explanation": "Sentence 1: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: (A) is not correct. -- Annotator 2 comment: _see succeeding comments_\n\nSentence 2: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: 1) Lojban has free word order. The predicate can come before, between, or after, its arguments.   1) “se” is not a verb. It is a function word that switches the 1st and 1nd arguments of the predicate it modifies. In (A), there is no predicate after “se”, which results 