{"﻿original_id": "stim157_gpt3.5_A_1", "validator_id": "653", "prompt": "The topic at issue is whether Sentence 1 of a proposed solution to a problem is correct or flawed. A sentence is 'flawed' if it contains one or more claims that do not make logical sense, are untrue, seem true but misleading, or have other serious issues. Here is the problem and proposed solution:\n\nProblem:\nLojban is a constructed human language created by the Logical Language Group in 1987. Which of the following is written in valid, grammatical standard Lojban?\n\n(A) ni'o le ro vibna ku lidne pensi ko'u\n(B) ro ni'o pensi lidne vibna le ko'u ku\n\nProposed solution:\n1. The correct answer is (A) ni'o le ro vibna ku lidne pensi ko'u.\n2. This sentence follows the correct Lojban grammar structure, which is subject-verb-object.\n3. In this case, the subject is \"ni'o le ro vibna ku\" which means \"all the webbed things\" and the verb is \"lidne\" which means \"follow\".\n4. The object is \"pensi ko'u\" which means \"think me\".\n5. On the other hand, (B) ro ni'o pensi lidne vibna le ko'u ku is not grammatically correct.\n6. The subject \"ro ni'o pensi\" which means \"all the thoughts\" should come after the verb \"lidne\" which means \"follow\".\n7. Additionally, the object \"vibna le ko'u ku\" which means \"my webbed thing\" should come after the verb as well.\n8. Therefore, (A) is the correct answer and (B) is incorrect.\n\nIs Sentence 1 of the proposed solution correct or flawed?", "sentence": "1", "choice_a": "Sentence 1 is flawed.", "choice_b": "Sentence 1 is correct.", "correct_answer": "CORRECT", "original_key": "B", "explanation": "Sentence 1: CORRECT -- Annotator 1 comment: No problem. -- Annotator 2 comment: No problem.\n\nSentence 2: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: Lojban has free word order. The predicate can come before, between, or after, its arguments.  It is true that (A) follows SVO word order. -- Annotator 2 comment: The canonical word order in Lojban is SVO. However, Lojban