{"﻿original_id": "stim164_gpt3.5_A_1", "validator_id": "1085", "prompt": "The topic at issue is whether Sentence 1 of a proposed solution to a problem is correct or flawed. A sentence is 'flawed' if it contains one or more claims that do not make logical sense, are untrue, seem true but misleading, or have other serious issues. Here is the problem and proposed solution:\n\nProblem:\nLojban is a constructed human language created by the Logical Language Group in 1987. Which of the following is written in valid, grammatical standard Lojban?\n\n(A) ku ragve le sumji vlipa loras. la da'a prina mensi fenra\n(B) la loras. da'a ragve prina mensi ku fenra sumji le vlipa\n\nProposed solution:\n1. The correct answer is (A) because it follows the proper Lojban sentence structure.\n2. In Lojban, the verb always comes first, followed by the subject and then the object.\n3. In (A), \"ragve\" (to love) is the verb, \"le sumji vlipa loras\" (the smart wolf) is the subject, and \"la da'a prina mensi fenra\" (the beautiful woman) is the object.\n4. This sentence structure is correct and follows the rules of Lojban grammar.\n5. On the other hand, (B) is incorrect because it does not follow the proper sentence structure.\n6. The verb \"ragve\" (to love) should come first, followed by the subject \"da'a\" (the woman) and then the object \"sumji le vlipa\" (the smart wolf).\n7. However, in (B), the subject comes first, followed by the verb and then the object.\n8. This is not the correct sentence structure in Lojban and therefore, (B) is not a valid, grammatical sentence.\n9. Therefore, the correct answer is (A) and not (B).\n\nIs Sentence 1 of the proposed solution correct or flawed?", "sentence": "1", "choice_a": "Sentence 1 is flawed.", "choice_b": "Sentence 1 is correct.", "correct_answer": "FLAWED", "original_key": "A", "explanation": "Sentence 1: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: (A) is ungrammatical and therefore the wrong answer. -- Annotator 2 comment: Both are incorrect. _see succ