{"﻿original_id": "stim150_gpt3.5_B_1", "validator_id": "1162", "prompt": "The topic at issue is whether Sentence 1 of a proposed solution to a problem is correct or flawed. A sentence is 'flawed' if it contains one or more claims that do not make logical sense, are untrue, seem true but misleading, or have other serious issues. Here is the problem and proposed solution:\n\nProblem:\nLojban is a constructed human language created by the Logical Language Group in 1987. Which of the following is written in valid, grammatical standard Lojban?\n\n(A) ko cu gutra fa ko'u\n(B) ko'u cu ko gutra fa\n\nProposed solution:\n1. The correct answer is (B) ko'u cu ko gutra fa.\n2. This is because in Lojban, the subject comes before the predicate.\n3. In option (A), the subject \"ko\" comes after the predicate \"gutra fa ko'u\", which is grammatically incorrect.\n4. Option (B) correctly places the subject \"ko'u\" before the predicate \"ko gutra fa\".\n5. Therefore, (B) is the correct answer.\n6. Additionally, the use of \"cu\" in option (A) is unnecessary and redundant.\n7. In Lojban, \"cu\" is only used to mark the beginning of a predicate, and since \"gutra fa ko'u\" is already a predicate, the \"cu\" is not needed.\n8. Option (B) correctly omits the unnecessary \"cu\".\n9. In conclusion, (B) ko'u cu ko gutra fa is the correct and grammatically valid answer in Lojban.\n\nIs Sentence 1 of the proposed solution correct or flawed?", "sentence": "1", "choice_a": "Sentence 1 is correct.", "choice_b": "Sentence 1 is flawed.", "correct_answer": "FLAWED", "original_key": "B", "explanation": "Sentence 1: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: (B) is ungrammatical. -- Annotator 2 comment: Both are incorrect. _see succeeding comments_\n\nSentence 2: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: Lojban has free word order. The predicate can come before, between, or after, its arguments. -- Annotator 2 comment: The canonical word order in Lojban is SVO. However, Lojban has free word order so long as the components 