{"﻿original_id": "stim189_gpt3.5_B_2", "validator_id": "1232", "prompt": "The topic at issue is whether Sentence 2 of a proposed solution to a problem is correct or flawed. A sentence is 'flawed' if it contains one or more claims that do not make logical sense, are untrue, seem true but misleading, or have other serious issues. Here is the problem and proposed solution:\n\nProblem:\nLojban is a constructed human language created by the Logical Language Group in 1987. Which of the following is written in valid, grammatical standard Lojban?\n\n(A) panje pu xanka cu surla loi le\n(B) le surla cu panje pu loi xanka\n\nProposed solution:\n1. The correct answer is (B) \"le surla cu panje pu loi xanka\".\n2. This is because in Lojban, the predicate (the verb or adjective) always comes before the sumti (the noun or pronoun).\n3. In (A), \"panje pu xanka\" is the predicate and \"loi le\" is the sumti, which is incorrect.\n4. In (B), \"panje pu\" is the predicate and \"loi xanka\" is the sumti, which follows the correct order.\n5. Therefore, (B) is the grammatically correct option.\n6. Additionally, \"le surla\" is a better choice for the subject than \"panje\", as \"surla\" is a more specific and concrete noun than \"panje\".\n7. This makes the sentence more clear and concise.\n8. Overall, (B) is the better answer because it follows the correct grammar rules and uses more specific and clear language.\n\nIs Sentence 2 of the proposed solution correct or flawed?", "sentence": "2", "choice_a": "Sentence 2 is correct.", "choice_b": "Sentence 2 is flawed.", "correct_answer": "FLAWED", "original_key": "B", "explanation": "Sentence 1: AMBIGUOUS -- Annotator 1 comment: No problem. -- Annotator 2 comment: Both are incorrect. _see succeeding comments_\n\nSentence 2: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: Lojban has free word order. The predicate can come before, between, or after, its arguments.   Also, #2 is asking for VS(O) word order, but (B) has SV(O) word order. This cannot end well. -- 