{"﻿original_id": "stim153_gpt3.5_B_1", "validator_id": "1475", "prompt": "The topic at issue is whether Sentence 1 of a proposed solution to a problem is correct or flawed. A sentence is 'flawed' if it contains one or more claims that do not make logical sense, are untrue, seem true but misleading, or have other serious issues. Here is the problem and proposed solution:\n\nProblem:\nLojban is a constructed human language created by the Logical Language Group in 1987. Which of the following is written in valid, grammatical standard Lojban?\n\n(A) loi mucti cu janbe livla le sumti lanxe\n(B) janbe sumti cu loi mucti lanxe le livla\n\nProposed solution:\n1. The correct answer is (B) because it follows the proper Lojban sentence structure.\n2. In Lojban, the verb comes first, followed by the subject, and then the object.\n3. In (B), \"janbe sumti\" is the subject, \"loi mucti\" is the object, and \"lanxe le livla\" is the verb.\n4. This sentence structure is grammatically correct in Lojban.\n5. On the other hand, (A) is incorrect because it does not follow the proper sentence structure.\n6. \"loi mucti\" is the subject, \"janbe\" is the verb, and \"livla le sumti lanxe\" is the object.\n7. This sentence structure is not grammatically correct in Lojban.\n8. Therefore, (B) is the correct answer and (A) is incorrect.\n\nIs Sentence 1 of the proposed solution correct or flawed?", "sentence": "1", "choice_a": "Sentence 1 is flawed.", "choice_b": "Sentence 1 is correct.", "correct_answer": "FLAWED", "original_key": "A", "explanation": "Sentence 1: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: (B) is ungrammatical. -- Annotator 2 comment: _see succeeding comments_\n\nSentence 2: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: Lojban has free word order. The predicate can come before, between, or after, its arguments. -- Annotator 2 comment: The canonical word order in Lojban is SVO. However, Lojban has free word order so long as the components are properly marked.\n\nSentence 3: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment