{"﻿original_id": "stim187_gpt3.5_A_2", "validator_id": "1572", "prompt": "The topic at issue is whether Sentence 2 of a proposed solution to a problem is correct or flawed. A sentence is 'flawed' if it contains one or more claims that do not make logical sense, are untrue, seem true but misleading, or have other serious issues. Here is the problem and proposed solution:\n\nProblem:\nLojban is a constructed human language created by the Logical Language Group in 1987. Which of the following is written in valid, grammatical standard Lojban?\n\n(A) cu fo'u cribe fo la .atlstan.\n(B) fo fo'u cu cribe la .atlstan.\n\nProposed solution:\n1. The correct answer is (A) cu fo'u cribe fo la .atlstan.\n2. This sentence follows the correct Lojban grammar structure, which is \"cu\" followed by the predicate, then the subject, and finally the object.\n3. In this case, \"cribe\" is the predicate, \"fo'u\" is the subject marker, and \"fo la .atlstan\" is the object.\n4. On the other hand, (B) fo fo'u cu cribe la .atlstan. is not grammatically correct.\n5. The subject marker \"fo'u\" should come before the predicate \"cribe\", but in this sentence, it comes after \"cu\".\n6. This violates the basic grammar rules of Lojban.\n7. Therefore, (A) is the only grammatically correct option and the correct answer to the question.\n\nIs Sentence 2 of the proposed solution correct or flawed?", "sentence": "2", "choice_a": "Sentence 2 is correct.", "choice_b": "Sentence 2 is flawed.", "correct_answer": "FLAWED", "original_key": "B", "explanation": "Sentence 1: AMBIGUOUS -- Annotator 1 comment: [No comment] -- Annotator 2 comment: Both are wrong. _see succeeding comments_\n\nSentence 2: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: The predicate marker “cu” does precede the main predicate of a clause, but in classical and standard grammars (CLL, BPFK), “cu” can only be used if there is a “term” before the predicate (an argument or a prepositional phrase). A structure like   cu [predicate] [subject] [object]  is