{"﻿original_id": "stim187_gpt3.5_B_2", "validator_id": "1577", "prompt": "The topic at issue is whether Sentence 2 of a proposed solution to a problem is correct or flawed. A sentence is 'flawed' if it contains one or more claims that do not make logical sense, are untrue, seem true but misleading, or have other serious issues. Here is the problem and proposed solution:\n\nProblem:\nLojban is a constructed human language created by the Logical Language Group in 1987. Which of the following is written in valid, grammatical standard Lojban?\n\n(A) cu fo'u cribe fo la .atlstan.\n(B) fo fo'u cu cribe la .atlstan.\n\nProposed solution:\n1. The correct answer is (B) fo fo'u cu cribe la .atlstan.\n2. This is because in Lojban, the verb \"cribe\" (to write) requires a direct object, which is \"la .atlstan.\"\n3. In option (A), the direct object \"la .atlstan\" is placed before the verb \"cribe,\" which is not grammatically correct in Lojban.\n4. In option (B), the direct object \"la .atlstan\" is placed after the verb \"cribe,\" which is the correct word order in Lojban.\n5. Therefore, (B) is the correct answer and (A) is incorrect.\n\nIs Sentence 2 of the proposed solution correct or flawed?", "sentence": "2", "choice_a": "Sentence 2 is flawed.", "choice_b": "Sentence 2 is correct.", "correct_answer": "FLAWED", "original_key": "A", "explanation": "Sentence 1: AMBIGUOUS -- Annotator 1 comment: No problem. -- Annotator 2 comment: Both are wrong. _see succeeding comments_\n\nSentence 2: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: - “cribe” means “bear” (“X is a bear of species Y”).  - There are no situations in Lojban where a direct object is required. All arguments can generally be omitted.  Lojban grammars also don’t have a concept of direct and indirect objects. -- Annotator 2 comment: {cribe} means \"is a bear\". \"To write\" is {ciska}. No Lojban predicates have parameters that are mandatory to be filled – any unfilled parameters are simply filled with the default elliptical value {ko'e} \"someone/thing/event/relation\".\n\nSentence 3: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: In (A), “(fo) la .atlstan.” is placed AFTER the verb “cribe”. Either position would be fine, though, because Lojban has free word order. -- Annotator 2 comment: The canonical word order in Lojban is SVO. However, Lojban has free word order so long as the components are properly marked.\n\nSentence 4: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: “la .atlstan.” is not a “direct object”. Even if “direct object” were used as a synonym of “second argument” (which would be a bad idea, because Lojban’s predicates aren’t regular enough for that to make sense; the patient-role argument isn’t always the second argument place), it would still be wrong, because “la .atlstan.” fills the fifth argument place of “cribe”, not the second. -- Annotator 2 comment: _see 3's comment_\n\nSentence 5: FLAWED -- Annotator 1 comment: The entire argument was based around a made-up rule about direct objects. Everything else about the sentences got ignored and the actual issues were missed. -- Annotator 2 comment: Both are wrong. _see previous comments_\n\n"}
